    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0415" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg317"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic">September 14,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 833.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 720, of the 22d ultimo, has been
                    received, and the Department is pleased with the frank declaration of Mr.
                    Delcassé that the policy of his Government is to preserve the unity of the
                    Chinese Empire and restore order therein, and to do nothing that will disturb
                    that entente between the powers which is so necessary at this crisis.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
